C.6 Provisional $\sigma_R$ under independence

The first $\sigma_R$ is computed by specializing Proposition 5 to zero covariances:
\sigma_R^{\mathrm{indep}} = \sqrt{\sum_{k=1}^{K} \sigma_k^2},


with each $\sigma_k$ obtained from Lemma 6 applied to the filtered MOE. This is reported as sigma_R_independence_flag=TRUE, alongside the components $\sigma_k$ and their sources. No inference is drawn from $\sigma_R^{\mathrm{indep}}$ without the flag being propagated.

